-- title:
--   Explicit bound on the time of the batched counting oracle: oTimeF ≤ K · n^2.99556085
-- statement:
--   Let $C_1,C_2,C_q,a_0,\kappa'\ge0$ be such that the preprocessing and query times of Theorem 30 (with pruned encodings) satisfy `tPreCoreP cShared30 P t` $\le C_1\,$`cost8p` and `tQueryAt` $\le C_2\,$`costQuery` under `Hyp30`, and the query cost at the parameters $c=20$, $\theta=56569/500000$ is at most $C_q D(m)^{q}\log D(m)$. Then for all $n,U,s,p$ with $1\le s\le n$, $p\ge1$, $\log n\ge20000$, $|\log s-0.0336175\log n|\le\log 2$, $\log p\le\log s+10^{-9}\log n$ and $\lfloor\log_2(U+1)\rfloor\le a_0+\kappa'\log n$,
--   $$\mathrm{oTimeF}(A,n,U,s,p)\le K_t(A,C_1,C_2,C_q,a_0,\kappa')\,e^{2.99556085\log n},$$
--   with the explicit constant `Kt`.
-- source:
--   Developed for the prove2.me APSP exponent campaign (https://prove2.me/campaigns/apsp-exponent) on top of the Lean formalization anthropics/formal-math, folder 3sum-apsp, commit e1a4e65 (https://github.com/anthropics/formal-math/tree/e1a4e6508154ea59f030480661590a9fe3018011/3sum-apsp; Lean v4.33.1, Mathlib v4.33.1). The statement comes from the file 3sum-apsp/ThreeSumApsp/Batch/OBound.lean of the campaign's modified copy of that library, which is not published; the new definitions it uses are in the platform definition bundles APSP2995561_Defs1 and APSP2995561_Defs2 (and APSP2996001_Defs1-2, APSP299791_Defs1-5 of the earlier entries). It follows the technical note "Deterministic APSP via thin products" (revised 7 October 2026) refining J. Alman and V. Vassilevska Williams, "Truly Subquadratic 3SUM and Truly Subcubic APSP via Triangles in Sparse Lopsided Graphs", arXiv:2610.06783v1 (https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.06783v1), Proposition 2.1 and Lemma 5.1 (the cost of a batched oracle call).

